<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:vm="using:Lightbox.App.ViewModels"
             x:Class="Lightbox.App.Views.LineOptionsBar"
             x:DataType="vm:MainViewModel">
  <!--
    B221. Simplify has existed, worked and been documented since phase 4c, and
    had no control anywhere: `lines.simplify` is in ShortcutMap with a null
    gesture, so it was bindable and unbound, and the manual said it lived "in
    the Arrow's options while you are inside a line" — a place nothing ever
    drew. A capability reachable only by an artist who first goes and invents a
    keybinding for it is one nobody finds.

    A collaborator rather than more of MainWindow.axaml, which is on the
    monolith ratchet — the trade BoneOptionsBar and GuideOptionsBar both made,
    for the same reason. The DataContext is inherited.

    Gated on the isolation session rather than on a tool, and that is the
    correction the manual needed as much as the control was: simplifying acts on
    the line you are *inside*, which is the white arrow's and the Width tool's
    state, not the black Arrow's. Showing it whenever either of those tools is
    merely in hand would be a button that does nothing until you have gone into
    a line.
  -->
  <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" VerticalAlignment="Center">
    <StackPanel.IsVisible>
      <MultiBinding Converter="{x:Static BoolConverters.And}">
        <Binding Path="PathEditActive" />
        <Binding Path="Workspace.QuickLineOptions" />
      </MultiBinding>
    </StackPanel.IsVisible>
    <TextBlock Text="{Binding IsolatedLineSummary}" VerticalAlignment="Center"
               ToolTip.Tip="How many points the line you are inside currently has." />
    <Button Content="Simplify" Command="{Binding SimplifyLineCommand}"
            ToolTip.Tip="Refit the line through fewer points. Press again to go further — each press is its own undo step, so one too many costs one Ctrl+Z." />
  </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
